<body>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="shell nav-shell">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="VizAI home"><span class="brand-sigil" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>VizAI</span></a>
      <button class="menu-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Open navigation" aria-expanded="false" data-menu-toggle><span></span></button>
      <nav class="primary-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation" data-primary-nav><a href="/#how-it-works">How it works</a><a href="/#services">Services</a><a href="/packages">Pricing</a><a href="/sample-report">Sample report</a><a href="/registry">Registry</a></nav>
      <div class="nav-actions"><a class="button-secondary" href="/portal" aria-current="page">Portal preview</a><a class="button" href="/scan">Run the free scan</a></div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="shell page-hero-grid">
        <div><div class="eyebrow">Managed work, clear authority</div><h1>Most of the work gets done for you. The decisions stay human.</h1></div>
        <div><p class="page-hero-copy">This separately planned customer workspace shows how managed reports, facts, evidence, and approvals could be organized without turning the marketing website into a full SaaS platform.</p><span class="sample-badge">Separate portal concept</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section compact">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head"><div class="section-kicker">Two sides of one governed workflow</div><h2 class="section-title">Switch between the customer workspace and your review queue.</h2><p class="section-copy">This is a concept for a separately built portal. It is not part of the current website release, and the controls do not log in, submit, approve, store, or publish anything.</p></div>
        <div class="portal-view-switch" aria-label="Portal preview view">
          <button class="active" type="button" data-portal-view="customer" aria-pressed="true">Customer view</button>
          <button type="button" data-portal-view="owner" aria-pressed="false">VizAI owner review</button>
        </div>

        <div class="portal-shell" style="margin-top:16px;">
          <aside class="portal-sidebar">
            <div class="portal-brand">VizAI · Portal</div>
            <div class="portal-nav"><span class="active">Overview</span><span>My source of truth</span><span>Fact review</span><span>Evidence</span><span>Reports</span><span>Findings</span><span>Tasks &amp; requests</span><span>Publication</span></div>
          </aside>

          <div class="portal-main">
            <div data-portal-panel="customer">
              <div class="portal-head"><div><h2>Northstar Logistics</h2><small>Infrastructure Maintenance · July 2026</small></div><span class="status-badge">Canon current</span></div>
              <div class="service-banner"><span class="service-avatar">VM</span><div><strong>VizAI maintenance is underway</strong><small>Running the monthly monitoring set, preparing the representation report, and tracking two corrections.</small></div><span class="status-badge">3 tasks active</span></div>
              <div class="portal-metrics">
                <div class="portal-metric"><span>Truth Canon</span><strong>v1.4</strong></div>
                <div class="portal-metric"><span>Open findings</span><strong>2</strong></div>
                <div class="portal-metric"><span>Your actions</span><strong>1</strong></div>
              </div>

              <section class="portal-panel" style="margin-top:12px;">
                <h3>Work in progress</h3>
                <div class="task-board">
                  <div class="task-row"><div><strong>Confirm reverse logistics description</strong><small>Proposed Canon update · due 24 Jul</small></div><span class="task-meta">Customer fact gate</span><span class="task-status customer">Your confirmation</span><button class="task-action" type="button">Review facts</button></div>
                  <div class="task-row"><div><strong>Monthly representation report</strong><small>Selected systems and agreed prompts</small></div><span class="task-meta">Maintenance service</span><span class="task-status working">In progress</span><button class="task-action" type="button">View progress</button></div>
                  <div class="task-row"><div><strong>Directory correction packet</strong><small>Former office listing · evidence attached</small></div><span class="task-meta">Managed improvement</span><span class="task-status review">Owner review</span><button class="task-action" type="button">View record</button></div>
                  <div class="task-row"><div><strong>Customs certification claim</strong><small>Authority-grade support is required</small></div><span class="task-meta">Evidence gate</span><span class="task-status customer">Needs evidence</span><button class="task-action" type="button">Add evidence</button></div>
                </div>
              </section>

              <div class="portal-content">
                <section class="portal-panel"><h3>Recent activity</h3><div class="activity-row"><span class="activity-dot"></span><div><strong>Canon v1.4 approved and published</strong><small>Owner approved · 18 Jul 2026</small></div></div><div class="activity-row"><span class="activity-dot"></span><div><strong>Monthly monitoring set completed</strong><small>Two material findings prepared · 15 Jul 2026</small></div></div><div class="activity-row"><span class="activity-dot"></span><div><strong>Headquarters evidence accepted</strong><small>Customer-supplied source passed review · 12 Jul 2026</small></div></div></section>
                <section class="portal-panel"><h3>Current priorities</h3><div class="finding-line"><i>1</i><div><strong>Former office listing</strong><small>Correction prepared; awaiting owner approval.</small></div></div><div class="finding-line"><i>2</i><div><strong>Service coverage</strong><small>Two newer services need stronger approved sources.</small></div></div><div class="finding-line"><i>✓</i><div><strong>Canonical record</strong><small>Customer-confirmed and technically valid.</small></div></div></section>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div data-portal-panel="owner" hidden>
              <div class="portal-head"><div><h2>VizAI review queue</h2><small>Paid deliverables and external actions requiring owner authority</small></div><span class="sample-badge">Owner console</span></div>
              <div class="review-summary">
                <div class="review-metric"><span>Ready for review</span><strong>3</strong></div>
                <div class="review-metric"><span>Work in progress</span><strong>5</strong></div>
                <div class="review-metric"><span>Waiting on customer</span><strong>2</strong></div>
                <div class="review-metric"><span>Approved today</span><strong>4</strong></div>
              </div>

              <section class="portal-panel" style="margin-top:12px;">
                <h3>Service work queue</h3>
                <div class="task-board">
                  <div class="task-row"><div><strong>Northstar · July Snapshot report</strong><small>Evidence ledger and findings attached</small></div><span class="task-meta">Snapshot service</span><span class="task-status review">Ready for review</span><button class="task-action" type="button">Review</button></div>
                  <div class="task-row"><div><strong>Northstar · Canon v1.5 update</strong><small>Reverse logistics description</small></div><span class="task-meta">Infrastructure build</span><span class="task-status customer">Customer confirmation</span><button class="task-action" type="button">View status</button></div>
                  <div class="task-row"><div><strong>Cedar &amp; Finch · Directory correction</strong><small>External submission packet prepared</small></div><span class="task-meta">Managed improvement</span><span class="task-status review">Ready for review</span><button class="task-action" type="button">Review</button></div>
                  <div class="task-row"><div><strong>Brightline · Monthly monitoring report</strong><small>Selected systems and observations</small></div><span class="task-meta">Maintenance service</span><span class="task-status working">In progress</span><button class="task-action" type="button">View progress</button></div>
                </div>
              </section>

              <div class="approval-card"><div><h3>Approval focus: Northstar July Snapshot</h3><p>VizAI completed source review, representation testing, evidence mapping, and the draft report. Customer-declared baseline facts are confirmed. Approval releases the deliverable to the customer; it does not guarantee an external-system outcome.</p></div><div class="approval-actions"><button type="button">View evidence</button><button type="button">Request changes</button><button class="primary" type="button">Approve deliverable</button></div></div>
              <div class="method-note"><strong>Authority boundary:</strong> Research, drafting, validation, monitoring, and action preparation remain separate from customer fact confirmation and final approval. A Canon or external action cannot move forward without the applicable human gate.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section tint">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head center"><div class="section-kicker">The operating model</div><h2 class="section-title">VizAI carries the workload. Authority remains explicit.</h2></div>
        <div class="role-flow">
          <article class="role-card"><span>Customer</span><h3>Declares and confirms</h3><p>Provides baseline facts, confirms proposed changes, and supplies evidence only where the claim requires it.</p></article>
          <article class="role-card vizai"><span>VizAI delivery</span><h3>Does the majority of the work</h3><p>Researches, structures, drafts, checks, monitors, and prepares the report, task, or external action.</p></article>
          <article class="role-card"><span>VizAI owner</span><h3>Reviews and approves</h3><p>Checks quality, evidence, scope, and policy before a paid deliverable or public action can move forward.</p></article>
          <article class="role-card"><span>Governed system</span><h3>Publishes and records</h3><p>Releases approved work, versions the Canon, and keeps an auditable change and approval history.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section dark">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head"><div class="section-kicker">Managed service delivery</div><h2 class="section-title">Each purchased outcome follows a defined workflow.</h2><p class="section-copy">Customers receive the work without having to operate software or manage the process themselves.</p></div>
        <div class="three-grid">
          <article class="info-card"><span class="card-icon">SP</span><h3>Snapshot</h3><p>Tests selected systems, reviews sources, prepares findings, and delivers a reviewed customer report.</p></article>
          <article class="info-card"><span class="card-icon">BL</span><h3>Infrastructure Build</h3><p>Structures customer-declared facts, maps evidence, and prepares the private Canon and public artifacts.</p></article>
          <article class="info-card"><span class="card-icon">MT</span><h3>Maintenance</h3><p>Runs the contracted cadence, tracks drift, prepares corrections, and routes exceptions to review.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="shell final-cta"><div><h2>The portal is the proof that VizAI is a managed service, not another dashboard to operate.</h2><p>Customers see their facts, evidence, work, and required decisions. VizAI performs the work and remains accountable.</p></div><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href="/packages">Review services</a><a class="button-secondary" href="/contact">Discuss the workflow</a></div></section>
